                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Transition metals are defined as elements that have, or readily form, partially filled "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "d"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " orbitals. Therefore groups 3-11, and lanthanides and actinides fit into this category."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "4193801913",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "d"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "-block elements consist of all the elements from group 3 through 12. Group 12 elements generally have full "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "d"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " orbitals and only occasionally will these be unfilled, even in ions."
                      }
